<header class="page-head">
  <h1>Settings</h1>
</header>

<p class="lede">
  Server configuration. Editable fields below take effect on the next apply.
  Structural values (VPN subnet, gateway IP, listen port, interface) are set at
  provisioning time in <code>naaf.conf</code> and shown read-only — changing them
  re-binds the listeners or invalidates every issued client config, so they need a
  re-provision rather than an edit here.
</p>

<h2 class="section">Endpoint &amp; DNS</h2>
<form method="post" action="/settings">
  <%= csrf_tag("/settings") %>

  <label class="field grow">
    <span class="label">Endpoint host <span class="hint">(FQDN clients dial; blank = use the raw IP below)</span></span>
    <input class="input" type="text" name="endpoint_host" value="<%= @settings[:endpoint_host] %>" placeholder="hub.example.test">
    <span class="help">When set, client configs use <code>&lt;host&gt;:<%= @settings[:listen_port] %></code> — move the box by repointing DNS, no config reissue.</span>
  </label>

  <div class="fields">
    <label class="field">
      <span class="label">Endpoint IPv4</span>
      <input class="input" type="text" name="endpoint_v4" value="<%= @settings[:endpoint_v4] %>" placeholder="203.0.113.10" required>
    </label>
    <label class="field">
      <span class="label">Endpoint IPv6 <span class="hint">(optional)</span></span>
      <input class="input" type="text" name="endpoint_v6" value="<%= @settings[:endpoint_v6] %>" placeholder="2001:db8::5">
    </label>
    <label class="field">
      <span class="label">MTU</span>
      <input class="input" type="number" name="mtu" value="<%= @settings[:mtu] %>" min="1280" max="1500" required>
    </label>
  </div>

  <div class="fields">
    <label class="field">
      <span class="label">DNS upstream</span>
      <input class="input" type="text" name="dns_upstream" value="<%= @settings[:dns_upstream] %>" placeholder="192.0.2.53" required>
    </label>
    <label class="field">
      <span class="label">Internal DNS domain</span>
      <input class="input" type="text" name="dns_domain" value="<%= @settings[:dns_domain] %>" placeholder="vpn" required>
    </label>
    <label class="field">
      <span class="label">WAN interface</span>
      <input class="input" type="text" name="wan_interface" value="<%= @settings[:wan_interface] %>" placeholder="eth0" required>
    </label>
  </div>

  <button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">Save &amp; apply</button>
</form>

<hr class="rule">

<h2 class="section">Read-only</h2>
<table class="table kv">
  <tbody>
    <tr><th>VPN subnet</th><td><code><%= @settings[:wg_subnet] %></code></td></tr>
    <tr><th>Gateway IP</th><td><code><%= @settings[:server_ip] %></code></td></tr>
    <tr>
      <th>SOCKS5 proxy</th>
      <td>
        <% if @proxy %>
          <code><%= h(@proxy) %></code>
          <span class="small muted">tunnel-only listen; follows the internet exit when one is up</span>
        <% else %>
          <span class="muted">disabled</span>
        <% end %>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr><th>Listen port</th><td><code><%= @settings[:listen_port] %></code></td></tr>
    <tr><th>WireGuard interface</th><td><code><%= @settings[:wg_interface] %></code></td></tr>
    <tr><th>Server public key</th><td><code><%= @settings[:server_pubkey] %></code></td></tr>
    <tr>
      <th>Last backup</th>
      <td>
        <% if @last_backup %>
          <code><%= @last_backup[:name] %></code>
          <span class="muted">(<%= @last_backup[:bytes] / 1024 %> KB)</span>
        <% elsif @backups_enabled %>
          <span class="muted">none yet</span>
        <% else %>
          <span class="muted">disabled</span>
        <% end %>
      </td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<p class="small muted">
  Snapshots live in <code><%= @backup_dir %></code> on the server and contain the
  server private key — they are mode 0600 and are deliberately not downloadable
  from here. Copy one with <code>scp</code>. See <code>docs/BACKUP.md</code>.
</p>

<p class="small muted">
  Certificates are not edited here. The store under <code>/etc/naaf/certs</code>
  is owned by provisioning (<code>deploy/provision/60-certs.sh</code>, DNS-01 only).
  See <code>docs/CERTS.md</code>. wstunnel, when enabled in <code>naaf.conf</code>,
  shows up as the <code>split·ws</code> config flavors on Clients.
</p>

<hr class="rule">

<h2 class="section">Change admin password</h2>
<p class="small muted">Replaces the only admin password. There is no second factor and no reset link.</p>
<form method="post" action="/settings/password">
  <%= csrf_tag("/settings/password") %>
  <div class="fields">
    <label class="field">
      <span class="label">New password</span>
      <input class="input" type="password" name="password" placeholder="new password (min 8 chars)" autocomplete="new-password" required>
    </label>
    <button class="btn btn-warn" type="submit">Update password</button>
  </div>
</form>
